  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Green Cities 2 W2 E2 - Bursa Water Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A senior unsecured loan of up to EUR 70.0 million to Bursa Water and Sewage  Administration (&quot;BUSKI&quot; or the &quot;Company&quot;) to finance the construction of a  c.67-km long water transmission line, a drinking water treatment plant (DWTP)  with a capacity of 300,000 m3/day and ancillary structures (the &quot;Project&quot;). The  loan will be co-financed by a concessional loan of up to EUR 5.0 million from  The Clean Technology Fund (&quot;CTF&quot;).  The Project will provide healthy and safe drinking water for the growing  population and industrial needs in the City of Bursa and contribute to a more  sustainable and energy efficient water resource mix by substituting the  extensive use of underground well water sources with surface water, which is  expected to reduce energy consumption.</narrative>
  </description>
